      "writtenOn": "2025-03-25T12:58:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e So this is disabled for key and arf frames?\n\nYes.\n\n\u003e This might be ok, but using the definition similar to frame_is_boosted() sounds more clear?\n\n   After regenerating speed-quality data using `frame_is_boosted()`, we observed \na mismatch in few contents with the current approach. We analyzed one of the test-case (\"SDR_Music_8b3y.y4m\" at 200kbps) and observed that the last two frames of video are coded at pyramid_level\u003d1 (without ARF frames).\nWith the current approach: filter_level is preserved when pyramid_level \u003e 1.\nWith frame_is_boosted(): filter_level is reset for the last two frames.\n\nSince this scenario is rare and is not thoroughly validated, we retained the current approach for now. Please let us know your opinion.",
      "parentUuid": "cabb0a3c_3a0cf8bf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 604,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 604,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "7b6d0e5c3938424de1ee61cd3a2c5d8039a89b08",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9dc56d82_6a0a9abe",
        "filename": "av1/encoder/speed_features.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 604,
      "author": {
        "id": 5185
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-25T23:57:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, the mismatch is wrt very short GOP for the last 2 frames?\nI feel limiting the filter level reset to pyramid_level \u003e 1 is to ensure generating good references for other frames, which might help with coding performance, right?\nIn this special case, maybe it makes sense to allow filter level reset. What do you think?\nLet\u0027s merge this CL for now. As we can see, the pyramid level doesn\u0027t closely align with frame quality as good as frame update type IMO (The meaning of one pyramid level can be different for different gop length). Maybe we should avoid to use it if possible.",
      "parentUuid": "2912075a_0de9614e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 604,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 604,
        "endChar": 52
      },
